rd-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Open an existing template or click the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2214\" data-start=\"2205\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">+ New</strong> button to create one.<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155057344862/original/fYwQcE9h_4V_3E56tL8LsrXCPkT6pSUj9g3cac.jpg?1761936370\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib inline-image\" data-id=\"155057344862\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; border: 0px; max-width: 100%; cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-left: 0px; display: block; text-align: left; width: auto;\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\"></p></li><li data-end=\"2326\" data-start=\"2239\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p data-end=\"2326\" data-start=\"2242\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">In the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2266\" data-start=\"2249\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Email Builder</strong>, click the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2298\" data-start=\"2278\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Add Elements (+)</strong> icon in the left sidebar.<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155057344863/original/ycOY6beqd0QuU3pv8n3JNYMu_vDTQXEzGQ10fe.jpg?1761936371\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib inline-image\" data-id=\"155057344863\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; border: 0px; max-width: 100%; cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-left: 0px; display: block; text-align: left; width: auto;\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\"></p></li><li data-end=\"2400\" data-start=\"2327\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p data-end=\"2400\" data-start=\"2330\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Locate the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2366\" data-start=\"2341\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Shopping Cart Element</strong> under the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2389\" data-start=\"2377\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Elements</strong> section.</p></li><li data-end=\"2492\" data-start=\"2401\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p data-end=\"2492\" data-start=\"2404\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Drag and drop the Shopping Cart Element into your desired section of the email layout.</p></li><li data-end=\"3039\" data-start=\"2493\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p data-end=\"2594\" data-start=\"2496\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Click on the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2534\" data-start=\"2509\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Shopping Cart Element</strong> to open the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"2555\" data-start=\"2547\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Edit</strong> tab on the left panel. Here you can:</p><ul data-end=\"3039\" data-start=\"2598\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 4px; margin-left: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 40px; line-height: 17px; list-style: disc;\"><li data-end=\"3039\" data-start=\"2933\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p data-end=\"3039\" data-start=\"2935\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><strong data-end=\"2965\" data-start=\"2935\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Adjust Layout and Spacing:</strong> Control padding, margins, and alignment to create a clean product grid.<br style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\"><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155057344864/original/ojdNHpASYmSeLg0HBLP70hmHEPsQOWGn8Afbdf.jpg?1761936372\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib inline-image\" data-id=\"155057344864\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; border: 0px; max-width: 100%; cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 5px; margin-left: 0px; display: block; text-align: left; width: auto;\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\"></p></li></ul></li><li data-end=\"3157\" data-start=\"3040\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p data-end=\"3157\" data-start=\"3043\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">(Optional) Use the&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"3076\" data-start=\"3062\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Visibility</strong> tab to configure&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"3121\" data-start=\"3094\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Device-Based Visibility</strong> or&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"3148\" data-start=\"3125\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Conditional Sending</strong> rules.</p></li><li data-end=\"3276\" data-start=\"3158\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><p data-end=\"3276\" data-start=\"3161\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Preview your email on&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"3194\" data-start=\"3183\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">desktop</strong> and&nbsp;<strong data-end=\"3209\" data-start=\"3199\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">mobile</strong> to ensure products display clearly and links function correctly.</p></li></ol><h2 class=\"ql-heading\" data-block-id=\"block-050a9542-2e1a-42f1-9c49-894ce943f862\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 35px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 1.5em; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px;\"><br style=\"box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 19.5px; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px;\"></h2>\n\t"}, {"slug": "155000004413-merging-multiple-records", "title": "Merging Multiple Records", "folder": "Contacts", "images": ["../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155038689655/original/msrC0ziRBWrwOgDlFUy-wpa50OzGcxwn7Qe374.png?1734694202", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155038676361/original/uGLPN-Upvogy9ALR5qvchypXQqliCVGCvw2615.png?1734686848", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155038676959/original/aWhjXtf2gfHWq2mP4E1kvPq7IUBA_waf5g31b5.png?1734687138"], "videos": [], "content": "\n\t\t<div class=\"ql-block\" data-block-id=\"block-8dbb4682-29fa-4331-ad30-a176086afafb\" dir=\"ltr\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(24, 50, 71); font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; display: inline !important;\">Merging contacts is a powerful way to clean up your database, eliminate duplicate records, and consolidate important information into one master record.&nbsp;</span></div><p>Merging helps:</p><ul><li>Eliminate duplicate entries.</li><li>Consolidate data into a single, accurate record.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Streamline communication and tracking.</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><p class=\"fd-toc\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TABLE OF CONTENTS</strong></p><ul><li><a href=\"#Step-1%3A-Select-Contacts-to-Merge\">Step 1: Select Contacts to Merge</a></li><li><a href=\"#Step-2%3A-Choose-the-Master-Record\">Step 2: Choose the Master Record</a></li><li><a href=\"#Step-3%3A-Review-and-Map-Fields\">Step 3: Review and Map Fields</a></li><li><a href=\"#Step-4%3A-Confirm-the-Merge\">Step 4: Confirm the Merge</a></li></ul><hr><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 30.63px; color: rgb(24, 50, 71); margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 1.17em; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px;\"><pre class=\"fd-callout fd-callout--note\" dir=\"ltr\">Merging contacts is a <strong>non-reversible</strong> action. Only admins have the access to merge contacts in a location. </pre></h3><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 30.63px; color: rgb(24, 50, 71); margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 1.17em; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px;\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Step 1: Select Contacts to Merge</strong></h3><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Go to the <strong>Contacts</strong> section of your CRM.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Select the contacts you want to merge by checking the boxes next to their names.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Click on the <strong>Merge</strong> icon on the top bar.</li></ul><pre class=\"fd-callout fd-callout--note\" dir=\"ltr\">You can only merge upto 10 contacts in one single merge. </pre><p><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155038689655/original/msrC0ziRBWrwOgDlFUy-wpa50OzGcxwn7Qe374.png?1734694202\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155038689655\"></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 30.63px; color: rgb(24, 50, 71); margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 1.17em; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px;\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Step 2: Choose the Master Record</strong></h3><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">In the merge preview screen, choose the <strong>Master Record</strong>.<ul><li>The Master Record is the primary record where consolidated data will be stored.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">All non-conflicting fields from other records will default to the Master Record\u2019s values.</li></ul></li></ul><p><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155038676361/original/uGLPN-Upvogy9ALR5qvchypXQqliCVGCvw2615.png?1734686848\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155038676361\"></p><p><br></p><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 30.63px; color: rgb(24, 50, 71); margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 1.17em; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px;\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Step 3: Review and Map Fields</strong></h3><ul><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Mandatory Field:</strong> Ensure you select a <strong dir=\"ltr\">Primary Email and Phone&nbsp;</strong>for the Master Record if there are additional email addresses and phone numbers that needed to be added in the contact.&nbsp;<ul><li dir=\"ltr\">If there\u2019s no Primary Email, remove additional emails and assign one as the primary to proceed.</li></ul></li><li dir=\"ltr\">For conflicting fields (e.g., phone numbers, addresses), choose the data you want to keep.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Information like <strong>Courses, Community Groups, and Products</strong> will automatically combine across all merged records. Other information like <strong>Activities, Payments, Orders, Invoices and Appointments</strong> will automatically default to the activity of the master record.</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 30.63px; color: rgb(24, 50, 71); margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 1.17em; text-indent: 0px; text-align: start;\"><strong dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: 700;\">Step 4: Confirm the Merge</strong></h3><ul style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 4px; margin-left: 0px; padding: 0px 0px 0px 40px; line-height: 17px; list-style: disc; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: -apple-system, &quot;system-ui&quot;, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Double-check your selections in the merge preview.</li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Click <strong>Merge</strong> to consolidate the selected contacts into one record.</li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Once merged, the data from non-master records will be consolidated into the Master Record, and the duplicates will be removed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155038676959/original/aWhjXtf2gfHWq2mP4E1kvPq7IUBA_waf5g31b5.png?1734687138\" style=\"width: 270px; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155038676959\"></p><p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;</p>\n\t"}, {"slug": "155000006378-help-guide-global-custom-colors", "title": "Help Guide: Global Custom Colors", "folder": "Brand Boards", "images": ["../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017307/original/NXta2BG8hoxRjGHcP3Jfh4ZBZTb0RAxc0gd695.png?1759329109", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017317/original/9Rq7vRFfIuHRkIFC1LvDMTimpMJFyrV8QAe2e8.png?1759329123", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017349/original/BhA0w3Kh7DT3C1PrwipPppYX7PA-NkeQzg7d5a.png?1759329137", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017450/original/e8KZj4eYKM7BALBMEBYXDgJ_fODWX-ee-Q3334.png?1759329206", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017366/original/3cnCwkqRRFbMRrVqki6pnW92G2r1LiwqJA5cb9.png?1759329149", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017432/original/scU-dOhADw-QxVKZg0H-nrMmcdu50lULhA5ce1.png?1759329188"], "videos": [], "content": "\n\t\t<p>Maintaining brand consistency across all your designs can be time-consuming. With <strong>Global Custom Colors</strong>, you can define your brand colors once and use them everywhere. Any updates to these colors instantly reflect across all your assets, saving you time and effort.<br><br><br></p><p class=\"fd-toc\"><strong>TABLE OF CONTENTS</strong></p><ul><li><a href=\"#What-Are-Global-Custom-Colors?\">What Are Global Custom Colors?</a></li><li><a href=\"#How-Are-They-Different-from-Design-Kit-Colors?\">How Are They Different from Design Kit Colors?</a></li><li><a href=\"#Benefits-of-Global-Custom-Colors\">Benefits of Global Custom Colors</a></li><li><a href=\"#How-to-Use-Global-Custom-Colors\">How to Use Global Custom Colors</a><ul><li><a href=\"#Step-1%3A-Open-Global-Settings\">Step 1: Open Global Settings</a></li><li><a href=\"#Step-2%3A-Add-or-Manage-Colors\">Step 2: Add or Manage Colors</a></li><li><a href=\"#Step-3%3A-Import-Colors\">Step 3: Import Colors</a></li><li><a href=\"#Step-3%3A-Use-in-Builders\">Step 3: Use in Builders</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"#FAQs\">FAQs</a></li></ul><h2 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"What-Are-Global-Custom-Colors?\"><br><strong>What Are Global Custom Colors?</strong></h2><p>Global Custom Colors are brand colors stored in <strong>Global Settings</strong> under <strong>Brand Boards</strong>.</p><ul><li><p>They are <strong>two-way synced</strong>, meaning if you update a color, it automatically updates in all the places it was used (emails, funnels, forms, pages, etc.).</p></li><li><p>By default, they appear in every <strong>color picker</strong> across the platform.</p></li></ul><h2 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"How-Are-They-Different-from-Design-Kit-Colors?\"><br><strong>How Are They Different from Design Kit Colors?</strong></h2><p><strong dir=\"ltr\"><br></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong dir=\"ltr\">Design Kit Colors</strong>: Quick-access colors available in the design builder. They <strong>do not sync</strong>, so updating them won\u2019t change existing designs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Global Custom Colors</strong>: Stored at the brand level with <strong>two-way sync</strong>. Update once, and the change applies everywhere that color is used.</p></li></ul><p><strong>In short:</strong> Design Kit = static quick access. Global Custom Colors = dynamic, synced brand consistency.</p><h2 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"Benefits-of-Global-Custom-Colors\"><br><strong>Benefits of Global Custom Colors</strong></h2><p><br></p><ol><li><p><strong>Consistency Across Assets</strong> \u2013 Maintain the same look and feel in all designs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Time-Saving</strong> \u2013 Update a color once, and it reflects everywhere.</p></li><li><p><strong>Easy Rebranding</strong> \u2013 Agencies can clone/share funnels, emails, and quickly rebrand new locations just by updating the global colors.</p></li><li><p><strong>Always Accessible</strong> \u2013 Global colors show up in every color picker.</p></li><li><p><strong>Quick Import</strong> \u2013 Bring in your existing custom values for faster setup.</p></li></ol><h2 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"How-to-Use-Global-Custom-Colors\"><br><strong>How to Use Global Custom Colors</strong></h2><h3 id=\"Step-1:-Open-Global-Settings\">Step 1: Open Global Settings</h3><ul><li><p>Navigate to <strong>Marketing \u2192 Brand Boards \u2192 Global Settings</strong>.<img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017307/original/NXta2BG8hoxRjGHcP3Jfh4ZBZTb0RAxc0gd695.png?1759329109\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155055017307\"><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017317/original/9Rq7vRFfIuHRkIFC1LvDMTimpMJFyrV8QAe2e8.png?1759329123\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155055017317\"></p></li></ul><h3 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"Step-2:-Add-or-Manage-Colors\">Step 2: Add or Manage Colors</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Add New Color</strong> \u2192 Give it a name and hex code.<img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017349/original/BhA0w3Kh7DT3C1PrwipPppYX7PA-NkeQzg7d5a.png?1759329137\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155055017349\"></p></li><li><p><strong>Edit</strong> \u2192 Update color details anytime.<img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017450/original/e8KZj4eYKM7BALBMEBYXDgJ_fODWX-ee-Q3334.png?1759329206\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155055017450\"></p></li><li><p><strong>Delete</strong> \u2192 Remove unused colors.</p></li></ul><h3 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"Step-3:-Import-Colors\">Step 3: Import Colors</h3><ul><li><p dir=\"ltr\">Click on New and then choose <strong>Import</strong></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\">Select the colors to import and proceed</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017366/original/3cnCwkqRRFbMRrVqki6pnW92G2r1LiwqJA5cb9.png?1759329149\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155055017366\"></strong><br></p></li></ul><p><br></p><h3 id=\"Step-3:-Use-in-Builders\">Step 3: Use in Builders</h3><ul><li><p>Open the <strong>Color Picker</strong> in emails, funnels, forms, or pages.</p></li><li><p>Your Global Custom Colors will appear automatically.</p></li><li><p>Use <strong>Manage</strong> inside the picker to add/edit colors on the fly.<img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155055017432/original/scU-dOhADw-QxVKZg0H-nrMmcdu50lULhA5ce1.png?1759329188\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155055017432\"></p></li></ul><h3 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"Brand-Colors-limitation-in-Email-Builder\"><br></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><strong>FAQs</strong></p><p><strong>Q: Will changing a Global Color update my existing assets?</strong><br>A: Yes. Global Custom Colors are two-way synced. Any change reflects instantly across all designs where that color is applied.</p><p><strong>Q: Why don\u2019t I see Global Colors in the color picker?</strong><br>A: The section only appears if you\u2019ve added at least one color in Global Settings.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Q: Can I import my existing custom value based colors?</strong><br>A: Yes. You can import them from the <strong>Custom Values</strong> section into Global Settings. This only creates a copy and does not lift and shift the custom value based colors.</p><p><strong>Q: How is this different from Design Kit colors?</strong><br>A: Design Kit colors are for quick access only and do not sync. Global Custom Colors sync across all assets.</p><p><strong>Q: Can agencies use this for client onboarding?</strong><br>A: Absolutely! Agencies can clone funnels/emails and simply update the Global Colors to instantly rebrand for new clients.</p>\n\t"}, {"slug": "155000001255-add-workflow-trigger-for-linkedin-lead-ads", "title": "Add Workflow Trigger For Linkedin Lead Ads", "folder": "Linkedin Lead Ads Integration", "images": ["../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670567/original/FjiBd5gOxs1U_01WZStGAPlYp0t3GLFJfg4f3c.png?1697806049", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670653/original/x9ZzK-IuPt8-OdP_yYtAyw19BewK1z-LEwb0df.png?1697806094", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670672/original/VBPUgcWHF1zBltucQz5iuOj_BhIXxsqSuwc018.png?1697806119", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670808/original/ul5g5Tu2Lv5gOwT6I6eYoCN_GyRz9Ohgxge3a9.png?1697806186"], "videos": [], "content": "\n\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\">In this guide, we will walk you through how to set up workflow automation for your LinkedIn lead ads integration.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><h2 dir=\"ltr\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Pre-requisite</strong></h2><p dir=\"ltr\">Please connect your Linkedin account with the CRM. To know more about how to connect Linkedin with the CRM, <a href=\"155000001151-integrating-linkedin-lead-ads-with-crm.html\">click here</a></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><br></p><h2 dir=\"ltr\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Add Workflow Trigger</strong></h2><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Go to \"Automation\" on the left menu and click on \"Create Workflow.\"<br><br></li><li dir=\"ltr\">Click on \"Add a new trigger\" and select the \"LinkedIn lead form submitted\" trigger.</li></ul><p><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670567/original/FjiBd5gOxs1U_01WZStGAPlYp0t3GLFJfg4f3c.png?1697806049\" style=\"width: auto;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib fr-bordered\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155010670567\"></p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Use filters to select a page/ad account (if you've added multiple ad accounts to the subaccount). If you can't see any ad accounts in the dropdown, ensure your LinkedIn account is integrated with the sub-account.</li></ul><p><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670653/original/x9ZzK-IuPt8-OdP_yYtAyw19BewK1z-LEwb0df.png?1697806094\" style=\"width: auto;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib fr-bordered\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155010670653\"></p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Use filters to select a specific form. Ensure that field mapping is completed for the chosen form; otherwise, the leads won't be fetched into the CRM.</li></ul><p><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670672/original/VBPUgcWHF1zBltucQz5iuOj_BhIXxsqSuwc018.png?1697806119\" style=\"width: auto;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib fr-bordered\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155010670672\"></p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">After setting the triggers, define the set of actions for the automation and save.</li></ul><p><img src=\"../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155010670808/original/ul5g5Tu2Lv5gOwT6I6eYoCN_GyRz9Ohgxge3a9.png?1697806186\" style=\"width: auto;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib fr-bordered\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"155010670808\"></p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Once the automation setup is complete, publish the workflow to activate it.</li></ul><p><br></p>\n\t"}, {"slug": "155000002072-pre-and-post-buffers", "title": "Pre and Post buffers", "folder": "Calendars", "images": ["../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155008252070/original/Pk23PglvoH7miofggGQhAj0wlNq9uHGckgb27d.png?1695296287", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155008249415/original/Ew_k9fwnbzOx3l7xgYOFgGaaAjPOgYVEfQc69a.png?1695295311", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155008248682/original/ZynVOHKf4olx_WfqBLTqWcqXZDeSk9T9uwd757.png?1695295018", "../../../../s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/155008248759/original/Hx5MxC2ya2FQPzRkH_BdOmFVw-zpDBL3NAa712.png?1695295045"], "videos": [], "content": "\n\t\t<p class=\"fd-toc\"><strong>TABLE OF CONTENTS</strong></p><ul><li><a href=\"#What-are-buffers?\">What are buffers?</a></li><li><a href=\"#How-to-set-buffers\">How to set buffers</a></li><li><a href=\"#How-to-turn-off-buffers%C2%A0\">How to turn off buffers&nbsp;</a></li><li><a href=\"#Buffer-Logic\">Buffer Logic</a></li><li><a href=\"#Buffer-Duration-Affecting-Available-Slots\">Buffer Duration Affecting Available Slots</a></li><li><a href=\"#FAQs\">FAQs</a></li></ul><h3 dir=\"ltr\" id=\"\"><br></h3><h3 dir=\"